# Container image rules (<% derived.option_labels.base_image %>)

- Multi-stage: build in a full-toolchain image, run in the smallest runtime image of the same family. Base image family: `<% options.base_image %>`; do not mix families (glibc vs musl packages are not interchangeable).
- Runtime images run as non-root, contain no shell or package manager, and expose only the app port declared in `.adlc/config.yaml`.
- Accept `ARG VERSION` and stamp it as the OCI label `org.opencontainers.image.version` and into the app (`/health` returns it) so `/adlc:verify` can compare running version to tag.
- No secrets, tokens or `.env` files copied into any layer; configuration arrives as environment variables at runtime.
- Each app has a `.dockerignore` excluding VCS, build output, tests fixtures and local env files.
- Templates and pinned tags: the `delivery-knowledge` skill, `references/base-image-<% options.base_image %>.md`.
